    <div class="note">
      <strong>Policy Relevance:</strong> The significant price spreads within each fuel type suggest that market transparency alone is not compressing prices to a narrow band. Consumers who do not actively compare prices risk overpaying substantially, which strengthens the case for interventions that promote price awareness at the point of purchase.
