    <p>The overall median lag of <strong>{fmt_hours(lag_overall_median)}</strong> indicates that most prices are captured shortly after retailer updates. However, <strong>{fmt_num(stale_count)}</strong> records ({fmt_pct(stale_pct)}) have lags exceeding 48 hours, and <strong>{fmt_num(very_stale_count)}</strong> ({fmt_pct(very_stale_pct)}) exceed one week. These stale records are concentrated across <strong>{fmt_num(stale_station_count)}</strong> stations, suggesting systematic under-reporting by a subset of retailers rather than occasional delays.</p>
    {"<p class='note'><strong>Data Note:</strong> A small number of records show negative update lag (source_updated_at is after recorded_at), which likely reflects clock skew between systems. These records were included in the analysis but do not materially affect the findings.</p>" if negative_lag_count > 0 else ""}

